            <ArticleTitle>A facile synthesis of reduced holey graphene oxide for supercapacitors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13225-13228</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc07475a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hydroxyl radicals (˙OH) generated from a UV/O3 solution reaction is used to efficiently etch graphene oxide nanosheets under moderate conditions. Reduced holey graphene oxide is directly used as a supercapacitor electrode material and exhibits high specific capacitance (224 F g-1 at a current density of 1 A g-1) and high volumetric capacitance (up to 206 F cm-3).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
